-- statement:
--   This bundle defines, over a field, the $q$-derivative $D_qf(x)=\frac{f(qx)-f(x)}{(q-1)x}$, the $q$-integer $[n]_q=\sum_{i<n}q^i$, the iterated $q$-derivative $D_q^n$, the $q$-factorial $[n]_q!=\prod_{i=1}^n[i]_q$, the $q$-falling factorial $[n]_q[n-1]_q\cdots[n-k+1]_q$, and the top $q$-Taylor term of $x^n$, namely $\frac{D_q^n(t^n)(x)}{[n]_q!}\,x^n$. These objects connect $q$-calculus to the partition-theoretic products of the book.
--
--   All divisions use Lean’s totalized field convention $a/0=0$. Precisely, the falling factorial is $\prod_{i=0}^{k-1}[n-i]_q$ with saturated natural subtraction; it is $0$ when $k>n$. Nonzero-denominator hypotheses occur in the separate theorems.
